WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.500
Episode 15

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.500
Desperate Escape<i>!!
</i>The Yamato in Alternative Space<i>!!</i>

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.500
( Air date: Jan 12, 1975 )

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.240
Space Battleship

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.240
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:45.070
In 2199, Earth was attacked by the mysterious
planet Gamilus with meteor bombs...

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:49.590
{SONO}...and mankind was facing extinction
due to the radioactivity in one year.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.070
{CHIKYUU}The space battleship Yamato, the first
Earth ship to exceed the speed of light...

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.120
...has departed for Iscandar to
obtain the radioactive purifier.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.920
Galactic System

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:17.720
Iscandar is located 148,000 light years
away in the Large Magellanic Cloud.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.720
Large Magellanic Cloud

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:26.170
Planet Balan

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.890
{GENZAI}Its current destination
is the mid-point, planet Balan.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.120
Yamato Second Bridge

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.540
Navigator, how about a break ?

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.750
Guys, I made
some coffee.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.670
Oh, thanks.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:51.660
Oh, well...

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.060
It never gets better,
Chief Life Environmental Commander.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.120
Great, it tastes so good.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.270
I feel so sorry for those who
can't drink coffee like this.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:10.590
I wish I could have someone who could
make coffee like this, as my wife.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.280
You're right.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.530
Should I propose ?

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.180
Mr. Ohta, do you want another ?

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.460
N...no, thanks.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.560
Ohta, you were forcing
yourself, weren't you ?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.580
You knew ?

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.580
Okay guys, stop wasting your
breath and get back to work !

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.520
Don't worry about me,
just make sure you plan right...

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.190
...so that the Yamato doesn't
fly into the middle of nowhere !

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.960
Don't worry about us.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.400
Hayashi, what's the error
factor to planet Balan ?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:36.660
Sir.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.070
Plus 3 degrees.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.380
Okay, adjust our course.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.410
Got it.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:51.360
Hey Shima, how many days will it take to get
from the mid-point, planet Balan, to Iscandar ?

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.770
Let's see...

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.840
On this course, it'll
take about 40 days.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.770
I see.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:03.580
But that's still 23 days behind schedule
from what Headquarters projected.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.170
I'll minimize the lost time,
and hurry up.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:11.780
Besides, Mori, please work hard,
so that you can make good coffee.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.870
Geez.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.800
Planet Balan

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.560
Gamilus Galactic System Base

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.020
Gale

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.110
Domel !

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.880
Domel !

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:50.720
Domel !

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.720
Domel !

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:57.570
This is planet Balan, located mid-way between
Earth and the Large Magellanic Cloud.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:02.070
Admiral Domel

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.370
A famed admiral
of Gamilus, Domel...

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:06.020
...just arrived as Commander of the Galactic
System sector, accompanied by his fleet.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.990
I'm Domel.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.990
Gale, I'll tell you the appointment
order from Lord Desler.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.520
The Commander of the
Magellan sector, Domel...

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.020
...has been assigned to command the
Galactic System sector as of January 5th.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.020
Gale, you will be under my
command as vice-commander.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.230
Say what ?

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.410
Gale, that was an order.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.120
This...

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.400
That...

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.370
And that...

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.550
Your lack of taste is the worst
on Gamilus !  It makes me puke !

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.160
Gale, replace all
the furniture.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.420
Gale...

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:58.880
...we'll begin an exercise in dimension 4,
sector 6, at 16:00.  Inform the fleet.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.070
A...aye, sir.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.190
Hey guys, don't
overlook any details.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:20.900
If we pamper it too much,
it'll be spoiled and useless...

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:22.970
...mustached commander.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.620
Besides, I wonder how many days have
passed since we entered deep space.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:32.560
The scenery doesn't change,
so I have no idea.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.500
The number of stars
has decreased.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.870
It's so vast that
it's almost uncanny.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:46.530
Hey, just give it up, everyone.
We don't know what's gonna happen.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.140
I've got goosebumps.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:52.190
Idiot.  It's too late
to worry about it.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.520
Hey, what's happening ?!

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:00.540
It's slowing down.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.270
Damn, what is the
driver doing ?

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:06.760
What happened ?!

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.870
I'm gonna go find out.
Kato, you take care of this.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:31.220
Chief Engine Operator Tokugawa, the
output of the Wave Motion engine is down.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.120
Report immediately.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.860
I'm trying to compensate,
but it's not working.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.870
Chief, the Wave Motion
engine has stopped.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.460
Switch to the sub-engines.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.210
Aye, sir.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.740
Hey Shima,
what happened ?

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:48.360
If I knew, we wouldn't
be in trouble.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.990
What's that mist ?

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.890
I'm analyzing it now.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.280
Engine room, what're you doing ?
Sub-engines, maximum thrust.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:13.290
I know.
Yabu, check the power.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:14.030
Aye, sir.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.110
I've checked three times, but
I can't get the power to come up.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.520
Analysis complete,
Chief Navigator.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:29.250
The main component of
the mist is hydrogen.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.060
What, hydrogen ?

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.050
Damn, it's finally calm.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:13.810
It looks
strange outside.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:15.810
Video panel on.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:30.140
I didn't expect the Magellanic
Stream to be around here.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:34.280
What ?  Hey Shima, what is
this "Magellanic Stream" ?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.210
Well, it's a stream of
hydrogen, so to speak.

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:42.520
The Magellanic Cloud was said to be
near the Solar System long time ago...

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.520
{GINGA}...but it passed by
the Galactic System...

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:48.170
{GINGA}...and moved to its current position,
trailing a stream of hydrogen.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:53.250
{SONO}Its width is several hundred million kilometers,
and its length is 164,000 light years.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.630
{DAITAI}That's just about
all we know.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:02.270
According to data, hydrogen volume
is 10 times that of the Sun...

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.070
{SUISO}...and the main channel of hydrogen
is flowing from the Magellanic Cloud...

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:06.860
{SUISO}...toward the Galactic
System at 200 km/sec.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:13.500
But this is unusual. We're not just
caught by the Magellanic Stream.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.270
What do you mean, Captain ?

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:18.990
We're trapped in a
fourth dimensional dislocation.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.990
Look at that.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.500
Ships that couldn't escape...

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.180
Are we going to
end up like them ?

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.290
Stop joking around.
Can't you do anything ?

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.060
Unidentified flying
object, detected.

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:49.030
It's an enemy ship.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.140
What ?
You found the Yamato ?

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:10.670
Yes, sir.

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:15.420
That Earth ship is capable of
flying in the fourth dimension, huh ?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:21.560
Even we have to hold exercises to prepare
for operations in the fourth dimension.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:28.490
Order the advanced scout to engage
the Yamato to draw their attention.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.670
Black Tigers,
prepare to take off.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.700
Main cannons,
prepare to fire.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.460
Chief Combat Commander, we can't use
Wave Motion energy in this situation.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.090
Use normal power, and do
it manually.  Manually !

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:49.380
Kodai, wait.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.510
What is it, Shima ?

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.900
Let's run away.
That's all we can do.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.320
Say what ?
Run away ?

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:57.970
Yes.  It's too reckless to engage
in combat in this unknown space...

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:02.520
...while we can't use
the Wave Motion engine.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:05.120
Shima, are you telling me
to show our back to the enemy ?

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.230
Captain, let me fight.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:11.240
If we run away from a ship like that,
it'll take advantage of our weakness.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:14.080
{KOUGEKI}It's said that a good
offense is the best defense.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.490
Let's run away.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:20.420
Shima is right.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:23.420
We run as much
as we can.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:26.490
Sub-engines, power up.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.450
Sub-engines, power up.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.340
Captain, there's only
one enemy ship.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.660
Kodai, that's an order.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.520
A report from
our advanced scout.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.040
The Yamato didn't counterattack,
it started running.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.500
What ?  They noticed it ?
How clever.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:13.730
All ships, head to the fourth 
dimensional cave.  Destroy the Yamato !

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.680
Gale, the Yamato is
smarter than expected.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.660
Why do you think it's running
away from a space destroyer ?

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:30.990
Dammit, the Yamato will be
destroyed at this rate.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.290
Nanbu, get the
main cannon ready !

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:36.660
An enemy fleet is approaching
from behind the Yamato !

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.230
It's estimated to be
one hundred thirty{three hundred}{thousand} ships !

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:50.210
Geez, no way, we can take on that !
Hey Shima, run !  Hurry !

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:51.320
This is the fastest !

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.490
Shima, calm down.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:59.970
Since we were able to enter here,
there should be an exit.

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.420
Find the escape route,
while running.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.170
Aye, sir.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.860
But the gauges are malfunctioning,
so it's nearly impossible to find the exit.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.870
Hey Shima, go faster, or the
Yamato'll look like a beehive !

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:47.560
Even if you say so, the
sub-engines have their limits !

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:53.530
We have to get away from them.
Kodai, stop their advance.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:54.720
Aye, sir.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.090
Nanbu, prepare
the main cannon.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:07.740
Fire.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:17.720
The rat is desperate.
But how long can they hold out ?

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.550
Gale, it's acting strange.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:22.120
Strange ?

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:27.560
Maybe the Yamato is still learning
about the dimensional dislocation.

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:28.770
Impossible.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:31.520
That Yamato...
Destroy the Yamato.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:33.630
Destroy it !
Don't give them any time !

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.290
Captain, if we continue running,
we'll stimulate their attack.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.330
Captain, the sub-engines
are reaching their limit.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.560
W...what's that ?

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:19.770
Our energy is gone.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:25.250
Those wrecked ships must've
been disabled because of this.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:39.070
Engine room !
Engine room !

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.170
Oh, no.

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.070
Captain !

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:09.460
What's happening ?

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:11.610
Strange.  None of the
other gauges are working.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:23.260
People of Earth,
I am Starsha of Iscandar.

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:31.270
I have been watching over
you since you left Earth.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:37.340
You have overcome
many hardships.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:44.630
I regard highly your love, courage and
determination to complete your duty.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:51.040
Guide the Yamato according
to the dimensional compass.

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:54.650
I'm Starsha of Iscandar.

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:02.580
It started working.

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.820
It's back to normal.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:10.960
Thank you, Starsha.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.550
Kodai, counterattack
as much as possible.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:23.190
Aye, sir.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:26.800
Shima, ahead full, in the
direction the compass shows.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.060
Aye, sir.
Ahead full.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:42.340
Fire ! Blow it to pieces !

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:53.160
Wave Motion engine, activated.

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:57.870
Good.  All hands, as soon as
we escape this hydrogen mist...

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.060
...we'll warp to get
away from the enemy.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.600
Activate the main engine.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.970
Activating the main engine.

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.620
Five minutes till warp.
Fasten seatbelts.

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:34.970
Hey Shima, hurry up.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.460
There's no effective damage at this rate.
It's like shooting a BB gun.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.560
Leaving the hydrogen mist.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.230
Wave Motion energy, 120%.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:55.900
Start the countdown.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:57.380
Fifteen...

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.250
...fourteen...

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.000
...thirteen...

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.170
...twelve...

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.060
Kodai, stop firing
the main cannon.

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:03.250
Stop firing the main cannon.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:08.680
...five...

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:09.350
...four...

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:10.140
...three...

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:10.970
...two...

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:11.970
...one...

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.230
...zero.
Start.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.260
The Yamato has warped.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.590
The Domel fleet failed...

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:57.780
It's a great relief to know
that Iscandar does exist.

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:00.460
Yeah, we can travel
more confidently.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:03.420
It's all thanks to you.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:05.930
What's wrong ?
You're acting weird.

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:10.420
If we fought head to head at that time, we don't
know what would've happened to the Yamato.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.420
Oh, c'mon, Kodai.

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:15.790
I didn't save the
Yamato from danger.

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:17.730
It was Starsha of Iscandar.

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:20.560
Good evening.

00:22:22.250 --> 00:22:23.890
What's wrong ?

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:26.570
Hey Shima, don't
tell me you're...

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:30.990
I like Starsha...

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:35.260
Starsha...?  I guess we'll remain
rivals for quite some time.

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:05.460
January 7th.  I encountered the Yamato,
and it shouldn't be taken lightly.

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:11.130
I encountered the Yamato,
and it shouldn't be taken lightly<i>!</i>

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.890
The space battleship
Yamato hurries to planet Balan.

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:20.930
Will it be storm or
rain that awaits them ?

00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:26.410
Hurry, Yamato. Earth is
waiting for your return.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:32.310
Only 273 days left until
the extinction of mankind.

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:35.910
273 days left till the destruction of Earth

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:43.390
Okita Juzo:

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:43.390
Naya Goro

00:23:43.670 --> 00:23:48.890
Mori Yuki:

00:23:43.670 --> 00:23:48.890
Asagami Yoko

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:54.400
Analyzer:

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:54.400
Ogata Kenichi

00:23:56.640 --> 00:24:06.140
Note:
Admiral Domel's ship, the Domelards II,
was originally a heavy battleship, bigger
than the Yamato.

00:23:56.640 --> 00:24:06.140
The tail was shortened, but the bow and
the bridge remained unchanged
after the redesign.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:16.140
Note:
On January 5th 2200, the 86th day, since the Yamato left Earth, it was caught by the Magellanic Stream, which actually exists and flows from the Magellanic Cloud to the Galactic System.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:16.140
Then it was trapped in an imaginary dimensional dislocation.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:26.140
Note:
The fighter Kato was maintaining was the Cosmo Zero, painted in Black Tiger scheme, but it didn't show up in the later episodes.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:26.140
The date after the escape from the
dimensional dislocation was January 7th.
273 days left.

00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:39.270
Translation

00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:39.270
Editing

00:24:39.270 --> 00:24:46.840
Timing

00:24:39.270 --> 00:24:46.840
Song Translations

00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:51.780
A
